<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="44143" href="schedule/2006/fall/LLS/496/44143.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2006" href="schedule/2006.xml">2006</calendarYear><term id="120068" href="schedule/2006/fall.xml">Fall 2006</term><subject id="LLS" href="schedule/2006/fall/LLS.xml">Latina/Latino Studies</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2006/fall/LLS/496.xml">Seminar in Latina/o Studies</course></parents><sectionNumber>DU </sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: "Chicanas and Latinas in the U.S."  Explores the experiences of Chicana and Latina women in the United States. Topics to be discussed include: history, civil rights movements, Chicana/Latina feminism, sexuality, religion, health, community activism, family, immigration, education, work, media, and artistic expression. Readings are drawn from interdisciplinary sources, but examined from a sociological perspective.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2006-08-23Z</startDate><endDate>2006-12-08Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>10:00 AM</start><end>11:20 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>331</roomNumber><buildingName>Gregory Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Dowling" firstName="J">Dowling, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>